4. DHCPv6
  4.1 DHCPv6 Operation Steps
      - Stateless DHCPv6 uses parts of SLAAC to ensure that all necessary information is supplied to the host.
      - Stateful DHCPv6 does not require SLAAC.
      - Steps for DHCPv6 operations:
        a. The host sends an RS message
        b. The router responds with an RA message
        c. The host sends a DHCPv6 SOLICIT message
        d. The DHCPv6 server responds with an ADVERTISE message
        e. The host responds to the DHCPv6 server
        f. The DHCPv6 server sends a REPLY message
  4.2 Stateless DHCPv6 Operation
      - Stateless DHCPv6 server is only providing information that is identical for all devices on the network such as the IPv6 adress of a DNS server.
      - The server is not maintaining any client state information(i.e., a list of available and allocated IPv6 addresses)
      - Stateless DHCPv6 server is only providing configuration parameters for clients, not IPv6 addresses.
  4.3 Enable Stateless DHCPv6 on an interface
      R1(config-if)# ipv6 nd other-config-flag
      R1(config-if)# end
      R1#
      R1# show ipv6 interface g0/0/1 | begin ND
  4.4 Stateful Operation
      - RA message tells the client to obtain all addressing information from a stateful DHCPv6 server, except the default gateway address which is the source IPv6 link-local address of the RA.
      - The server is maintains IPv6 state information.
  4.5 Enable Stateful DHCPv6 on an Interface
      R1(config)# int g0/0/1
      R1(config-if)# ipv6 nd managed-config-flag
      R1(config-if)# ipv6 nd prefix default no-autoconfig
      R1(config-if)# end
      R1#
      R1# show ipv6 interface g0/0/1 | begin ND

5. Configure DHCPv6 Server
5.1 DHCPv6 Router Roles
- Cisco IOS router can be configured to provide DHCPv6 server services:
a. DHCPv6 Server: Router provides stateless or stateful services.
b. DHCPv6 Client: Router interface acquires an IPv6 IP configuration from a DHCPv6 server.
c. DHCPv6 Relay Agent: Router provides DHCPv6 forwarding services when the client and the server are located on different networks.

5.2 Configure a Stateless DHCPv6 Server
- Enable IPv6 routing
  R1(config)# ipv6 unicast-routing
- Define a DHCPv6 pool name
  R1(config)# ipv6 dhcp pool IPV6-STATELESS
  R1(config-dhcpv6)#
- Configure the DHCPv6 pool
  R1(config-dhcpv6)# dns-server
  R1(config-dhcpv6)# domain-name example.com
  R1(config-dhcpv6)# exit
- Bind the DHCPv6 pool to an interface
  R1(config)# interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1
  R1(config-if)# description Link to LAN
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 address fe80::1 link-local
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 address 2001:db8:acad:1::1/64
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 nd other-config-flag
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 dhcp server IPV6-STATELESS
  R1(config-if)# no shut
  R1(config-if)# end
- Verify that the hosts have received IPv6 addressing information
  C:\PC1> ipconfig/all

5.3 Configure a Stateless DHCPv6 Client
- Enable IPv6 routing
  R3(config)# ipv6 unicast-routing
- Configure the client router to create an LLA
  R3(config)# interface g0/0/1
  R3(config)# ipv6 enable
- Configure the client router to use SLAAC
  R3(config-if)# ipv6 address autoconfig
  R3(config)# end
- Verify that the client router is assigned a GUA
  R3# show ipv6 interface brief
- Verify that the client router received other necessary DHCPv6 information
  R3# show ipv6 dhcp interface g0/0/1

5.4 Configure a Stateful DHCPv6 Server
- Enable IPv6 routing
   R1(config)# ipv6 unicast-routing
- Define a DHCPv6 pool name
   R1(config)# ipv6 dhcp pool IPV6-STATEFUL
   R1(config-dhcpv6)#
- Configure the DHCPv6 pool name
  R1(config-dhcpv6)# address prefix 2001:db8:acad:1::/64
  R1(config-dhcpv6)# dns-server 2001:4860:4860::8888
  R1(config-dhcpv6)# domain-name example.com
- Bind the DHCPv6 pool to an interface
  R1(config)# interface g0/0/1
  R1(config-if)# description Link to LAN
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 address fe80::1 link-local
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 address 2001:db8:acad:1::1/64
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 nd managed-config-flag
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 nd prefix default no-autoconfig
  R1(config-if)# ipv6 dhcp server IPV6-STATEFUL
  R1(config-if)# no shut
  R1(config-if)# end
- Verify that the hosts have received IPv6 addressing information
  C:\PC1> ipconfig/all

5.5 Configure a Stateful DHCPv6 Client
- Enable IPv6 routing
  R3(config)# ipv6 unicast-routing
- Configure the client router to create an LLA
  R3(config)# interface g0/0/1
  R3(config)# ipv6 enable
- Configure the client router to use DHCPv6
  R3(config-if)# ipv6 address dhcp
  R3(config)# end
- Verify that the client router is assigned a GUA
  R3# show ipv6 interface brief
- Verify that the client router received other necessary DHCPv6 information
  R3# show ipv6 dhcp interface g0/0/1

5.6 DHCPv6 Server Verification Commands
    R1# show ipv6 dhcp pool
    R1# show ipv6 dhcp binding

5.7 Configure a DHCPv6 Relay Agent
    Router(config-if)# ipv6 dhcp relay destination ipv6-address [interface-type interface-number]
    R1(config)# interface gigabitethernet 0/0/1
    R1(config-if)# ipv6 dhcp relay destination 2001:db8:acad:1::2 G0/0/0
    R1(config-if)# exit

5.7 Verify the DHCPv6 Relay Agent
    R1# show ipv6 dhcp interface
    R1# show ipv6 dhcp binding
    C:\PC1> ipconfig/all
